/**
 * Bundled open-source Google fonts, self-hosted via @fontsource.
 * Generated by scripts/gen-fonts.mjs - do not edit by hand.
 *
 * These are @font-face DECLARATIONS only. A browser does not fetch a woff2
 * until a rendered element actually uses that family, so declaring every face
 * costs a few KB of CSS, not megabytes of fonts. The service worker precaches
 * the woff2 files, so every family stays available with no network.
 *
 * Imported as JS modules rather than via CSS @import so each stylesheet passes
 * through Vite's module graph - which is what lets the build plugin strip the
 * redundant .woff fallback. Vite inlines CSS @import inside its own CSS plugin,
 * where transform hooks never see it.
 *
 * Latin subset only, which is what keeps each face around 15-25KB.
 */

